+## Loading-state correction, 2026-10-09
+
+Requirements RR06/V03/V05/Q01/R01/TD06/TD08. The owner reports a brief “No times yet” flash before the real histograms arrive. Previously `_finish_selection()` drew the newly selected track with an empty comparison snapshot before starting its optional read. Unknown data was presented as an empty population.
+
+`track_browser.gd` now reveals the selected track and both histograms together. A complete cache with the current 16-bin contract is shown immediately; an uncached selection retains the previous complete hero and charts until its response arrives. A first uncached view uses the existing small loading area. First-time service failures show “Comparison unavailable”; guests without cached comparisons see “Sign in to compare”. Only a successful, validated zero-population response shows “No times yet”. Successful reads clear the previous failure. Actual race availability remains independent of optional comparison reads, and local PBs remain visible for guest/offline entry. Existing selection/vehicle guards, deduplicated reads, unified driver field, exact server counts, five laps and public isolation remain intact.
+
+Changed files for this correction: `game/ui/track_browser.gd`, `game/tests/test_unified_histograms.gd`, `game/tests/test_menu_loading.gd`, this document, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md` and `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`. The existing menu test's guest-only delayed-board double now implements the production `signed_in` and `paged_discovery_available` capability methods; no assertion was removed. [Task-only Git checkpoint](evidence/free-race-histogram-loading-2026-10-09/scoped-change.patch).
+
+Actual verification through pinned `scripts/dev.ps1`, with isolated `APPDATA=build/free-race-histogram-loading-*-user` and `BMT_RESULTS_EVIDENCE=docs/evidence/free-race-histogram-loading-2026-10-09`:
+
+- `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_unified_histograms.gd -Graphical -CommandTimeoutSeconds 90`: **141 checks, zero failures**. Includes first frame, 24 individually observed delayed frames across two uncached tracks, warm cache, service failure, confirmed empty population, both charts/no personal times, optional racing and 11 native screenshots. [Log](evidence/free-race-histogram-loading-2026-10-09/histograms-final.log).
+- `TestApp -CommandTimeoutSeconds 90`: **99 checks, zero failures**, including stored PBs after an offline app relaunch. [Log](evidence/free-race-histogram-loading-2026-10-09/app-final.log).
+- `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_discovery_pages.gd -CommandTimeoutSeconds 90`: **269 checks, zero failures**, including 5,000-track browsing and selected-track availability. [Log](evidence/free-race-histogram-loading-2026-10-09/paging-final.log).
+- `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_menu_loading.gd -CommandTimeoutSeconds 90`: **38 checks, zero failures**, preserving coherent selection geometry and playable cached tracks while optional standings wait. [Log](evidence/free-race-histogram-loading-2026-10-09/menu-loading-final.log).
+- Scoped `git diff --check` and reverse Git checkpoint check: pass.
+
+The flash was reproduced before the fix: **80 checks, five failures** covering the first frame and both delayed selections. [Baseline log](evidence/free-race-histogram-loading-2026-10-09/before-fix.log). An initial overly broad reveal delay hid the offline app fixture's PB; guest/offline entry was corrected and the unchanged 99-check app suite passed. The menu fixture's missing cloud capability method was completed before its final pass.
+
+Inspected native [waiting](evidence/free-race-histogram-loading-2026-10-09/track-0-waiting.png) and [ready](evidence/free-race-histogram-loading-2026-10-09/track-0-ready.png) captures show the previous complete charts retained before the new hero appears. The fixture reuses retained verified Silmukka distributions and presentation-only synthetic track names; it is not a live catalog race or server write. Network data cannot be displayed before it arrives; cold selections wait to reveal, while compatible cached values appear immediately. No phone attachment check, physical-device test, Android export/install, full Validate, backend or production deployment was performed for this correction. Remaining acceptance: owner/device review of transitions under real service latency.
